  "body": "Part of #2607 (slice S4 of 6).\n\nThe order of the maintainer (2026-11-18): \"GPU shader issues get priority\".\n\n## What\nExtend the S2 kernel and the S1 CPU twin to the other sweep kinds of `crates/sim/src/stock_sim/field_sweep.rs` (lines 27-43):\n- true XY arcs (not chords);\n- bull nose, taper and drill tips (the golden-section minimum, 32 iterations, as `field_sweep.rs` lines 14-23);\n- shanked tools;\n- posed 4- and 5-axis moves and lathe moves (chords, as on the CPU).\n\nEach kind is added to the CPU f32 twin first, then to WGSL. A kind that is not ported still refuses by name.\n\n## Tests (CPU reference test for each kind)\n- One-sided parity for each kind: f32 twin against f64 `field_cut`, and GPU against the f32 twin on the software adapter.\n- A twin constant for each WGSL constant, as `trace.wgsl` and `cpu_eye.rs` do.\n\nSafety floor: stock simulation, `effort:max` for new algorithms.\n\nBlocked by #2627 (S2).\n\nDone means: each sweep kind of `field_sweep.rs` has a GPU kernel and a CPU twin with green parity tests, or a named refusal with a reason in the PR.\n\n",
